    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0559" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.6281/101: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-22T13:00:00+01:00">May 22, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. Legation’s 120, May 16.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d593-f1"/> Orgaz has now
                    replied to Legation’s note of May 18 requesting expulsion of German agents from
                    Spanish North Africa (see paragraph 6, section 1, Madrid’s 2430, May 4<anchor
                        n="73" xml:id="d593-f2"/>). He states he likewise is interested in execution
                    of Madrid agreement and that necessary measures have been taken for departure
                    from zone of Germans in question. He has ordered brief investigations of these
                        <pb facs="0560" n="548" xml:id="pg548"/> individuals to “guarantee strict
                    equity and justice.” As soon as necessary investigations are completed he will
                    inform Legation of their departure dates and respective routes. Department
                    should note that foregoing refers to German agents in Spanish Morocco and
                    Tangier as distinguished from German consular personnel in Tangier. Arrangements
                    for departure of last named are now in progress.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Algiers as our 38, repeated to Madrid as our 60.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
